Example rules, in priority order (they show the syntax; they are not a good schedule for this system):
```
{"condition": "pc1 = 2 & counter >= 10", "action": "p1"}
{"condition": "pc2 = 1 & coin2 = 0", "action": "p2"}
{"condition": "pc3 = 0", "action": "p3"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "p1"}
```
Rule 1 lets process 1 check once the counter has reached 10. Rule 2 lets process 2 write a tails coin. Rule 3 lets process 3 flip. The last rule is a catch-all default.
